The LICENSE and external scanner are from upstream tree-sitter/tree-sitter-ruby
at ad907a69da0c8a4f7a943a7fe012712208da6dee. This includes the upstream
heredoc serialization fix. The generated parser, node types and grammar
are unchanged from the release. Only a trailing blank line is removed
from the license text.

Local changes in src/scanner.c recognize anonymous block forwarding before
a closing parenthesis across whitespace and line comments, and symbol labels
ending in '?' or '!', including Ruby's otherwise reserved 'defined?'.
A comma directly after an anonymous block argument is invalid in MRI; the
scanner now rejects it. The other examples in the upstream block-argument case
retain their original trees.
See crates/hoonarqube-ruby/src/tests/parser_syntax.rs for boundary tests.
